      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Discussion on the Paper by Andrieu, Doucet and Holenstein",
      "bbox": [
        78.57550048828125,
        39.52751922607422,
        316.3913879394531,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the state has so high persistence it is known (Papaspiliopoulos et al., 2003) that the centred Gibbs sampler",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        57.378700256347656,
        438.2250671386719,
        65.6905517578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(for T =∞) has better mixing. The robustness of PG sampling is again very promising. Note that the SPF",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        66.5881118774414,
        438.2313232421875,
        75.65313720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and PMMH methods have worse performance for small values of the ratio, which is due to the deteriora-",
      "bbox": [
        42.70990753173828,
        77.30387115478516,
        438.2257995605469,
        85.61572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion of the bootstrap ﬁlter with decreasing observation error. This deterioration appears to have no effect",
      "bbox": [
        42.70990753173828,
        87.2664566040039,
        438.2266540527344,
        95.57830810546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on PG sampling in this simple setting.",
      "bbox": [
        42.70990753173828,
        97.22904205322266,
        186.81790161132812,
        105.5408935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Krzysztof Łatuszy´nski (University of Toronto) and Omiros Papaspiliopoulos (Universitat Pompeu",
      "bbox": [
        42.70990753173828,
        116.65653228759766,
        403.863037109375,
        124.9683837890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fabra, Barcelona)",
      "bbox": [
        42.7108154296875,
        126.6191177368164,
        109.93998718261719,
        134.93096923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We congraulate the authors for a beautiful paper. A fundamental idea is the interplay between unbiased",
      "bbox": [
        42.7108154296875,
        136.5817108154297,
        438.23138427734375,
        144.8935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "estimation (by means of importance sampling in this paper) and exact simulation. We show how unbiased",
      "bbox": [
        42.7108154296875,
        146.54429626464844,
        438.2276611328125,
        154.85614013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "estimation relates to exact simulation of events of unknown probability s ∈[0, 1]. Details, proofs and an",
      "bbox": [
        42.7108154296875,
        155.75369262695312,
        438.22601318359375,
        164.8187255859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "application to the celebrated Bernoulli factory problem (Nacu and Peres, 2005) can be found in Łatusz´nski",
      "bbox": [
        42.711700439453125,
        166.37083435058594,
        438.22412109375,
        174.78131103515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "et al. (2009).",
      "bbox": [
        42.71173095703125,
        176.4320526123047,
        89.78532409667969,
        184.743896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We wish to simulate the binary random variable Cs such that P[Cs =1]=s. If ˆS is a realizable unbiased",
      "bbox": [
        51.67812728881836,
        184.5298309326172,
        438.2230224609375,
        196.05160522460938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "estimator of s taking values in [0, 1], we use the following algorithm 1.",
      "bbox": [
        42.70977783203125,
        196.35740661621094,
        307.1163024902344,
        204.66925048828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 1: simulate G0 ∼U.0, 1/:",
      "bbox": [
        51.676177978515625,
        209.00906372070312,
        162.5209197998047,
        219.32046508789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 2: obtain ˆS:",
      "bbox": [
        51.676490783691406,
        217.8597869873047,
        114.61972045898438,
        228.03665161132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 3: if G0 ⩽ˆS set Cs :=1; otherwise set Cs :=0:",
      "bbox": [
        51.67648696899414,
        227.82252502441406,
        237.44578552246094,
        239.34439086914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 4: output Cs.",
      "bbox": [
        51.67633056640625,
        239.6501007080078,
        119.50189208984375,
        247.96200561523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If l1, l2, . . . and u1, u2, . . . are sequences of lower and upper bounds converging monotonically to s then",
      "bbox": [
        51.67646026611328,
        253.05491638183594,
        438.2233581542969,
        262.0811462402344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we can resort to the following algorithm 2.",
      "bbox": [
        42.710052490234375,
        263.017578125,
        203.8093719482422,
        271.3294372558594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 1: simulate G0 ∼U.0, 1/;set n=1:",
      "bbox": [
        51.67645263671875,
        275.66925048828125,
        197.70687866210938,
        285.98065185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 2: compute ln and un:",
      "bbox": [
        51.677398681640625,
        286.3849792480469,
        151.48655700683594,
        296.0419006347656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 3: if G0 ⩽ln set Cs :=1:",
      "bbox": [
        51.676177978515625,
        295.5945739746094,
        156.92498779296875,
        306.0044860839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 4: if G0 >un set Cs :=0:",
      "bbox": [
        51.676483154296875,
        305.5571594238281,
        159.31558227539062,
        315.9671936035156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 5: if ln <G0 ⩽un set n:=n+1 and go to step 2.",
      "bbox": [
        51.6766357421875,
        315.5198669433594,
        248.0857391357422,
        325.9299011230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Step 6: output Cs:",
      "bbox": [
        51.67680358886719,
        326.2356872558594,
        119.75296020507812,
        334.54754638671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We can combine these ideas to have unbiased estimators Ln and Un of ln and un. The estimators live on",
      "bbox": [
        51.67646789550781,
        343.62518310546875,
        438.2232666015625,
        353.28240966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the same probability space and have the following properties:",
      "bbox": [
        42.708984375,
        353.58819580078125,
        274.0151062011719,
        361.9000549316406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "P.Ln ⩽Un/=1",
      "bbox": [
        154.92349243164062,
        369.2191467285156,
        211.759033203125,
        379.53045654296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for every n=1, 2, . . . ;",
      "bbox": [
        245.23329162597656,
        369.2191467285156,
        326.0134582519531,
        378.2841796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
